# Tiger Style (skipprd)

Skill: **`tiger-style`**. SoT: root `AGENTS.md`. skipprd has no Cloud/ReAct kernel split; the engine is the product.

## Bar

- Encode invariants in the type system (`enum`, newtypes, `Option`/`Result`). Prefer compile failure over runtime “don’t call this wrong.”
- One type, CLI, catalog, and journal per job. Stringly dispatch, `rsplit`/`contains` to recover identity, and `serde_json::Value` hops at a typed API are illegal.
- Fail closed at trust boundaries. No silent defaults that pick a second path.
- Flat functions over one-implementor trait hierarchies. Shared logic in one place (DRY).
- Feature-gated code must compile: `cargo check --all-features` when touching `cfg(feature)`.
- Fixed safety ceilings in code. MUST NOT grow impl env knobs for pools/batches/timeouts the engine can bound itself.

## Anti-patterns

- Dual loaders/parsers/planners for the same job
- `legacy` / `compat` / `v1`/`v2` modules beside the surviving path
- Unbounded buffers “just for now”
- Treating “tests pass” as SoT if the old string path still compiles
